VITE_API_URL=https://shc-dashboard-api.azurewebsites.net

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mapbox (optional). Leave both commented out and the maps run entirely on the free layers --
# Esri satellite and OpenStreetMap -- exactly as they do today.
#
# Paste a PUBLIC token (starts with pk.) below and uncomment it. Mapbox Satellite then becomes
# the default basemap everywhere, with real detail past Esri's z18 ceiling. Vite inlines this at
# BUILD time, so it only takes effect after a push and redeploy -- setting it in Azure does
# nothing.
#
# Before using a token, in the Mapbox dashboard:
#   1. Add a URL restriction, and list EVERY domain the dashboard is served from. Today that is
#        https://shcriksu.co                                   <- the one people actually use
#        https://witty-pebble-05c3a8500.7.azurestaticapps.net   <- the Azure default hostname
#      The token is visible in the JS bundle (all pk. tokens are), and the restriction is the
#      only thing stopping someone else spending the quota. Miss a domain and Mapbox answers
#      403 for every tile from it -- the app then reports "Mapbox rejected the access token"
#      and falls back to the free layers, which looks like a broken feature rather than a
#      missing hostname.
#   2. Set a spending limit, or keep no card on file. The app's own tile budget is a per-browser
#      estimate, not a guarantee; the account is where the hard stop lives.
#
# VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=pk.xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Tiles one browser may draw from Mapbox per calendar month before the app drops back to the
# free layers on its own. Default 12,000, chosen as Mapbox's 200,000/month free tier spread
# across ~10 dashboard users with headroom. Raise it if far fewer people use the maps.
# VITE_MAPBOX_MONTHLY_TILES=12000
